source: crates/hydronode-cli/tests/c3_help.rs
expression: text
---
A fake HTTP device that sends plausible values on a schedule. It writes real
data into the sensor, so use a test sensor. Ctrl-C stops it.

Usage: hn simulate [OPTIONS] <SENSOR>

Arguments:
  <SENSOR>  Sensor id (use a test sensor)

Options:
      --kind <KIND>   What the fake device measures [default: weather] [possible values: weather, greenhouse, random]
      --every <SPAN>  Time between rounds, at least 10s [default: 30s]
      --count <N>     Stop after this many rounds
      --secret-stdin  Read the sensor secret from stdin
  -h, --help          Print help

Global options:
  -p, --profile <NAME>  Profile to use (server and login), see 'hn profile list'
      --json            Print JSON instead of tables (stable shape, for scripts)

Examples:
  hn sensors create "Test device"
  hn simulate <sensor-id> --kind weather
  hn simulate <sensor-id> --kind greenhouse --every 1m --count 10
